# rerun_queue.tsv — queue of bake-off candidates that need (re-)measuring.
#
# Consumed by test/bakeoff/run_queue.sh. Copy this file to
# test/bakeoff/rerun_queue.tsv (gitignored — do not commit real entries) and
# fill in real rows.
#
# Format:
#   - TAB-separated.
#   - Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.
#   - Columns (exactly 3, TAB-separated): execution	consensus	reason
#       execution  execution client id, e.g. geth / nethermind / erigon / reth /
#                  besu / nimbus_eth1 / ethrex
#       consensus  consensus client id, e.g. prysm / lighthouse / teku /
#                  nimbus / lodestar / grandine
#       reason     free-text note on WHY this row needs a rerun (fix landed,
#                  prior run crash-looped, anchor poisoned, etc.) — shows up
#                  in the queue log and in --dry-run's plan output.
#
# Example rows (uncomment + edit; each row is run via
# test/bakeoff/run_candidate.sh <execution> <consensus>):
#
# geth	prysm	rerun after extract_archive -o fix (97541bd)
# nethermind	lodestar	rerun: lodestar pruneHistory CLI-flag fix (77d939d)
# erigon	teku	rerun: previous row crash-looped before the watchdog existed
